#
# DERIVED-ARITHMETIC rescores: releases 6, 7 and 8 recomputed OFFLINE (zero API
# calls) with the verifier that reads a claim's own stated arithmetic. Evidence
# was rebuilt by verify.build_evidence over each row's recorded hits and notes
# and the reconstruction was checked against the recorded claims.evidence_keys
# first: 86 of 86 reproduce exactly, 0 mismatches, in all three releases.
# 86 not 89: `abs-fp999`, `fr-fp999-abstain` and `abs-offtopic` are guard
# answers that hold no hits and no claims block at all — production's guard
# path returns before build_evidence — so there is nothing in them to rescore
# and scoring them would mint claims the run never verified.
# Deterministic mode, so `claims` here is not comparable to the recorded
# production block beside it (`claims_recorded`, judge on); the comparison
# these files exist for is against the same rescore taken on the tree before
# the change. Measured that way: release-6 supported 154/169 -> 155/169,
# release-7 158/173 -> 159/173, release-8 173/188 unchanged, and the two rows
# that move are both `fu-compare-those`'s derived difference and nothing else.
# The frozen release files are untouched.
